# Line endings are not cosmetic in this repository.
#
# The SQLite plugin on the device splits a migration into statements itself,
# and it does it with `split(";\n")`. A file checked out with Windows line
# endings has ";\r\n", never splits, and the phone is handed one enormous
# statement it cannot run — with nothing about the SQL looking wrong.
#
# Git on Windows converts to CRLF on checkout by default (core.autocrlf), so
# a fresh clone would produce exactly that. This pins every text file to LF in
# the working tree, which is also what `tools/db/device-sql.test.mjs` checks.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched: they are not text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
